  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cambodian Climate Financing Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CCFF programme is a unique climate financing facility, designed to accelerate nationally determined contribution (NDC) implementation while addressing both financial and non-financial gaps in Cambodia. It aims to scale up climate finance in Cambodia through providing long-term concessional financing for high-impact climate projects.

&#x2022; The programme aims to catalyse private sector capital and provide financial additionality in resource-constrained priority sectors from nationally determined contribution sectors.
&#x2022; It aims to scale up private sector climate finance through de-risking investments, showcasing commercial viability and addressing market gaps (lack of long-term financing, perception of high risk for climate projects).
&#x2022;  The programme will address non-financial barriers including policies and regulations to ensure the sustainability of the programme and climate financing in Cambodia.</narrative>
  </description>
